The former does not imply the latter.  Even on "no-teleport levels",
you can zap a /teleport at other creatures and they'll be ported away
succesfully.  You just can't teleport yourself.

> My main problem is that as soon as I go up the stairs I get slimed. The
> first time I read my scroll of fire, and that was cool, but now I've got
> nothing. So all I can do is pray.

A /fire would be ideal.  Slimes respect elbereth.  My ploy would
probably be to make sure I can pray succesfully and try to find a
permanent E source (/fire or /lightning) or, failing that, a semi-perm
one (athame, /digging) and go upstairs, teleport the minotaur away, and
write E on the stairs.  Then you can take the monsters out at a more
leisurely pace (be careful if it's a semi-perm E).

If you have /tele and no semi or permanent E source, you can at least
run up, teleport the minotaur away, and finger-E.  Try to use
spells/wands to take out the slimes with many finger-E's in place.

And, of course, have a plan for if the minotaur returns (more /tele
charges or run away if you can't take him down at range).

Also bear in mind that minotaurs are susceptible to sleep.



